  "implementationDetails": {
    "audioStrategy": "Single AudioContext architecture unifying Organ (Layers A/B sharing one Organ FX chain + dedicated Rotary routing), Piano (Layers A/B with Timbre EQ, model voicing, and independent/grouped FX chains), and Synth (Layers A/B/C with independent/grouped FX chains and deterministic Arpeggiator/Gate). Every layer traverses the exact ordered Layer Effects chain (Mod 1 -> Mod 2 -> Delay -> Amp Sim/EQ -> Compressor -> Reverb) -> [Direct | Shared Rotary Speaker with morphable speed] -> Layer level -> Master Bus -> Master Level Gain -> Soft-Knee Limiter -> Brickwall Safety Clipper -> single Destination. Grand (78 stereo OGG), Upright (52 stereo OGG), Rhodes Mk I (15 mono OGG), and Wurlitzer EP200 (25 mono OGG) are bundled recorded cuts from inputs/samples/ (170 files total). Organ engines (B3/B3 Bass, Vox, Farf, Pipe 1/Pipe 2), Synth engine (Pure/Sync/Multi/Super/FM-H), Clav/Digital/Misc piano types, sympathetic string resonance, reverb impulse responses, and the labeled sample-failure fallback are live/generated Web Audio synthesis.",
    "generatedSources": 8,
    "sampleSources": 4
  },
